# Architecture

See `CONTEXT.md` (root) and `services/{name}/CONTEXT.md` for current system and service state.

## Monorepo layout

- Each service is an independent deployable under `services/{name}/`
- New service: add folder under `services/`, own `README.md`, own dependency manifest (`pom.xml`, `package.json`, etc.)

## Domain-driven layout (within a service)

Each domain module owns its layers:

```
{domain}/
  controller/
  service/
  service/impl/
  repository/
  model/entity/
  model/dto/
  model/enums/
  model/valueobject/
```

## Layer rules

- Controller → service only
- Service → repository only
- No cross-domain direct calls — use shared types in `shared/` when needed
- No cross-service code imports — services communicate via API only

## Temporary implementations

- `InMemory*Repository` classes are temporary; mark with `// TODO: Remove` javadoc until real persistence exists
